  m_Name: 1900s hawkers
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: 'Hawker Culture 1900s '
  info: "Hawker stalls began as makeshift street setups in the early 20th century,
    serving affordable, home-style meals to workers. These evolved into organized
    hawker centers in the 1960s, offering dishes like satay, laksa, and char kway
    teow. Today, hawker culture is celebrated as a UNESCO-recognized tradition that
    encapsulates Singapore\u2019s culinary diversity and communal dining ethos.  "
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4a4ae438d3b4b47c7996954f2fbb7f3c, type: 3}
